               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgMetropolitan0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgMetropolitan0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Ornamental profile of a warrior. © The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>The arrival in Abya Yala (America) - In this text, we will explore different studies on the period when the first peoples could have arrived in <i>Abya Yala</i> (America) (<htcite1>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgMetropolitan1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgMetropolitan1', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Deep Vessel. © The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York (<htcite2>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Jōmon Period (縄文) - initial historical period characterized by vessels with cord markings (jōmon). (<htcite3>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
